DIJKSTRA’S ALGORITHM
(Shortest Path in a Weighted Graph)
1️⃣ Problem Statement

You are given a weighted graph with V vertices and E edges.
Each edge has a non-negative weight.

Your task is to find the shortest distance from a given source vertex to all other vertices.

👉 If a vertex is not reachable, its distance should remain infinity (∞).

2️⃣ Why Dijkstra’s Algorithm?

Used when all edge weights are non-negative

Very common in interviews, maps, network routing

Greedy algorithm

Time-efficient using Priority Queue

3️⃣ Real-World Example

📍 Google Maps finds the shortest route from your location to all destinations.

4️⃣ Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Initialize distance[] array with ∞

Set distance[source] = 0

Use a Min Heap / Priority Queue

Pick vertex with minimum distance

Relax its neighbors
→ update distance if shorter path found

Repeat until queue becomes empty

